      "content": "/*\n    This program solves Laplace's equation on a regular 2D grid using simple Jacobi iteration.\n\n    The stencil calculation stops when (err >= CONV_THRESHOLD OR iter >= ITER_MAX).\n*/\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f\n\ndouble **grid;\ndouble **new_grid;\nint size;\nint iter_max_num;\n\ndouble absolute(double num) {\n    if (num < 0)\n        return -1.0 * num;\n    return num;\n}\n\nvoid allocate_memory() {\n    grid = (double **)malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\n    new_grid = (double **)malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n        grid[i] = (double *)malloc(size * sizeof(double));\n        new_grid[i] = (double *)malloc(size * sizeof(double));\n    }\n}\n\nvoid initialize_grid() {\n    int center = size / 2;\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++) {\n            if (i >= linf && i <= lsup && j >= linf && j <= lsup)\n                grid[i][j] = 100;\n            else\n                grid[i][j] = 0;\n            new_grid[i][j] = grid[i][j];\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nvoid save_grid() {\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++) {\n            fprintf(stdout, \"%lf \", grid[i][j]);\n        }\n        fprintf(stdout, \"\\n\");\n    }\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]) {\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &size);\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &iter_max_num);\n\n    int hasError = 1;\n    int iter = 0;\n\n    allocate_memory();\n    initialize_grid();\n\n#pragma omp parallel shared(hasError, iter, grid, new_grid, size, iter_max_num)\n    {\n        while (hasError && iter < iter_max_num) {\n#pragma omp master\n            hasError = 0;\n#pragma omp barrier\n\n#pragma omp for schedule(static) reduction(| : hasError)\n            for (int i = 1; i < size - 1; i++) {\n                for (int j = 1; j < size - 1; j++) {\n                    new_grid[i][j] = 0.25 * (grid[i][j + 1] + grid[i][j - 1] +\n                                               grid[i - 1][j] + grid[i + 1][j]);\n\n                    double errorCurrent = absolute(new_grid[i][j] - grid[i][j]);\n                    if (errorCurrent > CONV_THRESHOLD)\n                        hasError = 1;\n                }\n            }\n\n#pragma omp master\n            {\n                double **previous_grid = grid;\n                grid = new_grid;\n                new_grid = previous_grid;\n                iter++;\n            }\n#pragma omp barrier\n        }\n    }\n\n    save_grid();\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/laplace_seq.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Eliminating the second work-sharing copy sweep through ping-pong buffers reduces per-iteration synchronization and memory traffic while preserving every Jacobi state and output byte.",
  "notes": "Both buffers start with identical fixed boundary values, so pointer swapping retains the original boundary behavior even for small valid grids. Master/barrier phases keep all threads synchronized at loop boundaries.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Initialize both buffers identically, then swap their pointers after each stencil sweep instead of copying every interior cell.",
    "Replace single-region coordination with master/barrier coordination while retaining static row partitioning and the boolean OpenMP reduction."
  ]
}
